 "literal": "Please spare, may you live, O north wind! Like a snake's / hanging sloughed skin resembling, pure white waterfall's / high mountain situated near, that very amla tree's / herd of wild cows grazing courtyard / grass-thatched hut, of the good woman's town.",
 "translation": "May you prosper, O north wind! Please spare the town of my beloved, she of the grass-thatched hut with a courtyard where herds of wild cows graze on amla fruits, situated near the high mountain where a pure white waterfall cascades, resembling the sloughed skin of a snake.",
 "modern": "வடகாற்றே! நீ வாழ்க! பாம்பின் சட்டை போன்ற தூய வெள்ளை அருவிகள் விழும் உயர்ந்த மலையின் அருகில் உள்ளது நெல்லி மரங்கள் நிறைந்த பகுதி. அங்குள்ள முற்றத்தில் காட்டுப் பசுக்கள் நெல்லிக்காய்களை மேயும். அத்தகைய புல்லால் வேயப்பட்ட குடிலைக் கொண்ட என் நல்லவளின் ஊரை நீ வருத்தாமல் காப்பாயாக.",
 "explanation": "This poem is set in the pālai (wasteland/separation) landscape, spoken by the hero who is traveling away from his beloved. He addresses the chilly north wind, which intensifies the pain of separation for lovers. He begs the wind to be gentle and spare his beloved's humble village from its freezing blast. Her village is described as having grass-thatched huts where herds of wild cows graze on fallen amla fruits in the courtyards. This peaceful settlement is nestled near a high mountain featuring a pure white waterfall that resembles a discarded snake skin. Through these vivid natural images, the hero expresses his deep love and anxiety for his beloved's well-being during the cold season.",
